      "incorrect_belief": "Open-loop control can reliably achieve a specific distance regardless of external factors like battery voltage, floor friction, or load changes.",
      "correction": "In open-loop control, the system executes a pre-determined command (e.g., 60% power for 2 seconds) without measuring the result. Consequently, any variation in battery voltage, floor friction, or load will cause the actual distance traveled to deviate from the intended target."
