      "citations": [2, 3],
      "name": "Proportional control",
      "incorrect_belief": "Using a proportional controller alone will always allow the rover to reach the exact target distance with zero error.",
      "correction": "A proportional controller sets the motor command based on the current error (u(t) = Kp * e(t)). However, as the rover approaches the target, the error becomes very small, resulting in a motor command too weak to overcome static friction. This causes the rover to stop short of the target, creating a non-zero steady-state error."
